Short source-landscape note: the 2023 documentary universe for Félix Tshisekedi in Chapter 3B is dominated by UN human-rights and security reporting, international and local NGO reporting on protest repression, detention, torture, and impunity, Congolese legal and gazette materials on emergency powers and victim protection, and local-news coverage of the Kinshasa and Goma protest crackdowns. The strongest source families for later inspection are UNJHRO/MONUSCO, OHCHR treaty-body and special-procedure records, Amnesty/HRW/CPJ/RSF, official Congolese laws and decrees, and reputable local outlets such as Radio Okapi and Actualité.cd.

